{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>YHWH your Elohim you shall fear; Him you shall serve, and to Him you shall cleave, and by His name you shall swear.</b> 'You shall fear' — lest you transgress a negative commandment; 'Him you shall serve' — in a positive commandment; 'and to Him you shall cleave' — that you not separate your thought from Him." "<b>And the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote:</b> It is possible regarding men of this rank, who possess the merit of devekut (cleaving), that their soul is bound in the bond of life even in their lifetime, for they themselves are a dwelling-place for the Shekhinah, as the author of the Kuzari hinted. Up to here." "<b>And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted:</b> 'YHWH your Elohim you shall fear' — to include Torah scholars. And this statement was made by Rabbi Akiva, and it was fitting for him to say it, for he was among those who entered the Pardes and entered in peace and came out in peace; and concerning him it is said (Song of Songs 1:4): ״משכני אחריך נרוצה״." "<b>By way of the Kabbalah,</b> the Sage intended in this verse the Ḥokhmah, as it is written (Job 28:28): ״(הן) יראת אדני היא חכמה״; and for the honor of that hidden Ḥokhmah, which the wise of the earth understand, he interpreted it thus. And he would interpret a great matter — every occurrence of את in the Torah, for they contain exalted secrets and mighty mysteries pointing to the wonders of perfect faith. And in the manner that they interpreted (Numbers 7:1): ״להקים את המשכן״ — to include another Mishkan that was established with it; (Genesis 21:1): ״וה׳ פקד את שרה״ — to include the other barren women, teaching that all the barren women were remembered together with her; and so likewise all the occurrences of את in the Torah, each one of them containing a glorified matter. And who is wise and will understand these, who is discerning and will know them?" "<b>And by His name you shall swear.</b> After all these qualities are in you, then you may swear by His name. Or, 'and by His name you shall swear' may be a positive commandment for specific times and appointed occasions when there will be sanctification of the Name through this, in the manner that we find with Elijah and Ḥoni ha-Me'aggel." "<b>By way of the Kabbalah.</b> ״את ה׳ אלהיך תירא״ — that is fear, which thought cannot grasp; and ״ואותו תעבד״ — that is wisdom. And thus we find in the Yerushalmi: ״ואותו תעבד״ — Him and His Torah. That is the Torah that preceded the world by two thousand years. ״ובו תדבק״ — understanding, for there is the return of the souls; and ״ובשמו תשבע״ — the tongue is sated with satiation (shevi'ah)." "<b>And behold,</b> all is alluded to in this verse (Ecclesiastes 7:19): ״from ten rulers who were in the city,״ and similarly they are alluded to in the verse (I Chronicles 29:11): ״לך ה׳ הגדולה והגבורה והתפארת והנצח וההוד כי כל בשמים ובארץ לך ה׳ הממלכה,״ the meaning being that all that is between the heavens and the earth is that He is the peace that decides (makhri'ah); and likewise all of them are further alluded to in Song of Songs 5:15 — Song of Songs 5:15 — in the verse (Song of Songs): ״שוקיו עמודי שש מיוסדים על אדני פז,״ its meaning being that His thighs are pillars of six, and behold they are eight: יסוד and אל״ף דל״ת — behold, all is alluded to in this verse; and similarly in the verse (Proverbs 8:22): ״ה׳ קנני ראשית דרכו,״ which speaks of when there were no תהומות and mountains and earth; and this is clear."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {6 "The phrase 'שירים ה׳:ט״ושירים' appears to be a dittography or copyist duplication of the Song of Songs reference (5:15), rendered as found."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:31.373424192Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}